---
import Machine from "../components/Machine.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="llmcpu"
  description="A computer whose CPU is a language model: it runs poems, photographs, noise and real programs alike, in your browser."
>
  <div class="intro">
    <h1>A computer whose CPU is a language model</h1>
    <p>
      Give it anything: a poem, a photograph, random noise, or a real program. A small language model, running on your
      graphics card, reads the bytes a few at a time, decides what each instruction means, and carries it out on a
      little machine with memory, registers and a console. There is no wrong reading. Watch what it makes of them, and
      what the program turns out to do. If you hand it a real RISC-V program you can also run a silicon processor
      alongside and see where the two part ways.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Machine />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
  }

  .intro p {
    font-size: var(--step1);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
